      "content": "The holes appearing \"magically\" could be indicative of another more elusive pest, such as leafhoppers. They are very small and can be difficult to spot. In addition, another cause might be natural leaf spot diseases where tiny depressions form due to fungal infections. Greenhouse mildew or sooty mold are possibilities. Consider using a barrier spray containing EcoSafe, or a horticultural oil for better control. You'll also want to ensure the greenhouse environment is well-ventilated to discourage the growth of pathogens. Perform a thorough inspection of your plants, perhaps even disassemble a leaf or two to inspect among the veins, as pests can hide there too. Don't overlook the potential of non-biological causes, such as light scorching from too close proximity to a heat source or a physical object damaging the leaves mistakenly. Keep monitoring and you may also want to try an integrated pest management (IPM) approach for long-term control.",
